<br>

Draw the histograms with the population standard deviation on top (using `geom_vline()`):


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
ggplot(data = tibble(sd_unbiased)) +
  geom_histogram(aes(x = sd_unbiased),
                 color = "black", fill = "white",
                 bins = 12) +
    geom_vline(xintercept = pop_stats$pop_sd,
             col = "red", linetype = "dashed") +
  labs(title = "Histogram of estimated unbiased standard deviations",
       subtitle = "Population standard deviation shown in red",
       x = "Unbiased sd")
```

